WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:03.410
- I couldn't get any entry
level job in my own company

00:00:03.410 --> 00:00:05.230
'cause I couldn't pass the written test

00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:07.010
or the math test for the two disciplines.

00:00:07.010 --> 00:00:08.050
I couldn't.

00:00:08.050 --> 00:00:10.860
I own the whole fuckin' thing
and the straight facts are

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:13.395
I could not work for my own
company in an entry level job.

00:00:13.395 --> 00:00:15.812
(soft music)

00:00:20.024 --> 00:00:22.300
- Were you always successful?

00:00:22.300 --> 00:00:24.060
- In every thing but school.

00:00:24.060 --> 00:00:24.930
- Didn't do well in school?

00:00:24.930 --> 00:00:27.063
- Poor, terrible actually.

00:00:28.070 --> 00:00:28.903
Punted it.

00:00:34.738 --> 00:00:36.650
And this is where I give
my parents enormous credit.

00:00:36.650 --> 00:00:38.870
Education's the way out for immigrants.

00:00:38.870 --> 00:00:39.703
- Sure is.

00:00:39.703 --> 00:00:43.590
- My mom recognized that I was
a merchant, an entrepreneur.

00:00:43.590 --> 00:00:46.310
And then when I got D's
and F's, she punished me.

00:00:46.310 --> 00:00:49.040
Even though she knew I didn't
need school, in her heart,

00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:52.160
she made me know that there
was accountability for things.

00:00:52.160 --> 00:00:54.750
The biggest problem
right now is insecurity.

00:00:54.750 --> 00:00:57.250
Everybody's actions are to get shit

00:00:57.250 --> 00:00:58.910
to close their insecurity.

00:00:58.910 --> 00:01:03.300
You've so much time and
everybody's in such a rush.

00:01:03.300 --> 00:01:04.530
They're in a rush because they want

00:01:04.530 --> 00:01:06.630
to prove something to somebody.

00:01:06.630 --> 00:01:08.790
Money is not the variable of happiness.

00:01:08.790 --> 00:01:11.270
To me, life is broken down
into complaining and not.

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:13.310
So if you're not complaining,

00:01:13.310 --> 00:01:15.344
well then I have no advice for you.

00:01:15.344 --> 00:01:17.200
I'm pumped, you did it.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:20.770
I just don't understand people
dwelling and complaining.

00:01:20.770 --> 00:01:24.070
Like listen, I really really
really would have enjoyed

00:01:24.070 --> 00:01:25.900
being the quarterback of the New York Jets

00:01:25.900 --> 00:01:27.960
but by fourth grade I looked
around, I'm like, fuck,

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:29.200
I'm not gonna be the
quarterback of the Jets.

00:01:29.200 --> 00:01:30.100
(audience laughing)

00:01:30.100 --> 00:01:31.298
And so I said, you know what?

00:01:31.298 --> 00:01:33.450
Instead of being the
quarterback of the Jets,

00:01:33.450 --> 00:01:34.580
I'm gonna buy the Jets.

00:01:34.580 --> 00:01:36.700
There's so many people
that are talking shit

00:01:36.700 --> 00:01:38.810
about how big of an
entrepreneur they're gonna be

00:01:38.810 --> 00:01:40.410
and how much they're gonna achieve

00:01:40.410 --> 00:01:42.110
and they don't work on weekends.

00:01:42.110 --> 00:01:44.060
The reason I do a daily vlog on YouTube

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:46.100
is don't listen to what I'm saying,

00:01:46.100 --> 00:01:47.200
watch what I'm doing.

00:01:47.200 --> 00:01:50.060
I want to make patience
and empathy and gratitude

00:01:50.060 --> 00:01:53.940
and eating fuckin' dog
shit for 15 years, cool.

00:01:53.940 --> 00:01:55.180
Period.

00:01:55.180 --> 00:01:56.440
Because that's the only
way they're gonna get it.

00:01:56.440 --> 00:01:57.620
- Right.

00:01:57.620 --> 00:01:59.848
- You know I worked every
Saturday in my 20's.

00:01:59.848 --> 00:02:03.130
I don't sit on my couch and
say, I'm gonna be a millionaire

00:02:03.130 --> 00:02:05.460
and then jerk off while
I'm playing Madden all day.

00:02:05.460 --> 00:02:07.560
People want all these
special things to happen,

00:02:07.560 --> 00:02:09.730
but then they're acting
like everybody else.

00:02:09.730 --> 00:02:12.942
And that gets into the
Saturdays in your 20's.

00:02:12.942 --> 00:02:16.051
Or just taking risks or
things of that nature.

00:02:16.051 --> 00:02:18.330
This shit's fuckin' binary.

00:02:18.330 --> 00:02:21.430
Either you do the shit that
gets you there or you don't.

00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:23.770
And everybody's focused
on the finish line,

00:02:23.770 --> 00:02:26.740
not the treadmill work and
drinkin' the fuckin' egg

00:02:26.740 --> 00:02:28.050
like Rocky fuckin' Balboa.

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:29.150
They don't want to do that shit.

00:02:29.150 --> 00:02:30.520
- So what should we do, Gary Vee?

00:02:30.520 --> 00:02:32.525
- People should stop
fuckin' stop complaining.

00:02:32.525 --> 00:02:34.800
People should figure out
who the fuck they are.

00:02:34.800 --> 00:02:37.450
You've got to figure out how to try shit.

00:02:37.450 --> 00:02:39.904
Like that's the only, you just never know

00:02:39.904 --> 00:02:42.260
what your favorite food
was until you tried it.

00:02:42.260 --> 00:02:43.730
You only had chicken
you might not have known

00:02:43.730 --> 00:02:45.720
that hot dogs were the best.

00:02:45.720 --> 00:02:47.510
So, that's what I love about the internet.

00:02:47.510 --> 00:02:50.563
These kids have so much option
to watch shit on YouTube.

00:02:51.620 --> 00:02:55.040
My only answer, is just, try shit.

00:02:55.040 --> 00:02:57.020
The reason most people who
are listening right now

00:02:57.020 --> 00:02:58.620
are not doing that thing,

00:02:58.620 --> 00:03:00.582
is they're worried about
the opinion of somebody,

00:03:00.582 --> 00:03:05.120
usually their mother,
usually their father.

00:03:05.120 --> 00:03:08.140
And the reality is is that your spouse

00:03:08.140 --> 00:03:09.620
may be the person holding you back

00:03:09.620 --> 00:03:11.170
and you have to have that conversation.

00:03:11.170 --> 00:03:12.660
- Do you feel like you judge yourself?

00:03:12.660 --> 00:03:13.493
- I don't.

00:03:13.493 --> 00:03:15.170
And it's what I want for everybody else.

00:03:15.170 --> 00:03:16.553
We're beating ourselves up.

00:03:17.560 --> 00:03:19.899
Everybody sucks at something.

00:03:19.899 --> 00:03:20.732
Right?

00:03:20.732 --> 00:03:22.660
Like we all have short comings.

00:03:22.660 --> 00:03:23.980
And we all have strengths.

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:26.290
And for me it's like why
don't we just audit that.

00:03:26.290 --> 00:03:28.230
You have to love hard.

00:03:28.230 --> 00:03:30.620
You have to love eating shit.

00:03:30.620 --> 00:03:32.479
You have to love people leaving comments

00:03:32.479 --> 00:03:35.070
saying, you suck.

00:03:35.070 --> 00:03:36.620
You have to love the process.

00:03:36.620 --> 00:03:37.940
Figure out what your fuckin' thing is

00:03:37.940 --> 00:03:39.596
and stop making fucking bullshit excuses

00:03:39.596 --> 00:03:42.691
who the President is, your mom did this,

00:03:42.691 --> 00:03:45.750
I missed it, I had that idea for Uber.

00:03:45.750 --> 00:03:47.380
Then why didn't you fuckin' do it, dick?

00:03:47.380 --> 00:03:49.333
People decide no before they try.

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:55.420
You just decided no because
the system tells you no.

00:03:55.420 --> 00:03:57.240
You've been sold no.

00:03:57.240 --> 00:03:59.560
If you're lucky enough
right now to be listening

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:02.460
and you're good at what you like,

00:04:02.460 --> 00:04:05.040
become tunnel fuckin' vision.

00:04:05.040 --> 00:04:06.832
Because there's way too
many voices telling you

00:04:06.832 --> 00:04:08.210
what and how.

00:04:08.210 --> 00:04:09.260
I want the pain.

00:04:09.260 --> 00:04:10.370
I want the process.

00:04:10.370 --> 00:04:12.000
I have the patience.

00:04:12.000 --> 00:04:13.770
I don't care when I have setbacks.

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:16.570
I know that I'm asking
for something special.

00:04:16.570 --> 00:04:18.090
And if you're asking for something special

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:19.720
it should be hard.

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:20.913
Everybody's saying no.

00:04:23.370 --> 00:04:25.010
I just say yes.

00:04:25.010 --> 00:04:26.810
And then if it's a no,
I don't give a fuck.

00:04:26.810 --> 00:04:28.280
You gonna judge me that I lost?

00:04:28.280 --> 00:04:29.420
I don't give a fuck what you think.

00:04:29.420 --> 00:04:31.310
And that's why I get so into that.

00:04:31.310 --> 00:04:33.870
Because then you're not scared to try shit

00:04:33.870 --> 00:04:34.960
because when you don't give a fuck

00:04:34.960 --> 00:04:37.120
what everybody says about you failing.

00:04:37.120 --> 00:04:38.010
You love failing.

00:04:38.010 --> 00:04:38.863
I love the music.

00:04:39.730 --> 00:04:40.950
Own your shortcomings.

00:04:40.950 --> 00:04:41.783
Own your strengths.

00:04:41.783 --> 00:04:44.370
Surround yourself with the other shit

00:04:44.370 --> 00:04:46.560
and stuff starts to pop.

00:04:46.560 --> 00:04:47.597
Thank you for having me.

00:04:47.597 --> 00:04:50.764
(audience applauding)

